From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: a check on the back for every write the loop skip drops (EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY), off by default

What: EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY compares the front's registers with the back's, and a skipped write
leaves them equal, so it cannot show a draw lost by EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP (0600). With
EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY=1 the front skips nothing: each write the skip would drop is sent as
before, and right before it (a Call entry, neutral for fast draw reuse) the back checks, in stream
order, that CallMethod would have ignored it: the 3D method sink is empty (#488's condition), the
shadow RAM and the register already hold what the write leaves, the front's value is the back's,
and for draw.end the draw manager is in an instance loop. A write that fails any of these is a
difference. Zero differences over a walk is the proof that the skip loses nothing there.
Timing changes in verify mode (an extra Call entry per would-be skip, and nothing skipped), so
judge fps with EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 alone.

Switch: EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY=1 (exact "1", boot, read when the split front is made), only with
EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 working (same-value skip on). Off: one test of a front member, taken only on a
write the skip drops. EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY=1 can run beside it.
Log (HW_GPU): at start "EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY=1: nothing is skipped; ..." (Info); then
"EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY: N would-be skips checked on the back, D differences" (Info) at the first
check, every 4 Mi checks and with each of the first 8 differences, which also get a Warning
"EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP_VERIFY difference: method ... draw mode ...". The EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP lines keep
counting, as would-be skips. Pass: N in the millions, D = 0.

Origin and credit: our own, for zortos293/Lichii 7e2a9fe20c (#178, Thibaut LÉAUX) and 5ba52f7720
(#488, Marc Stampfli) as ported in 0600.
---
